{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784147432,"nonce":"0/6gf07kj8GtxGD88MtN3E4OG1M=","title":"The **Run-Pipeline flow** in the SolidJS UI (ADR-0028): select a pipeline and see the mandatory/optional parameters it dictates, fill a typed form, and dispatch — the headline ask that started ADR-0043.","message":"Scope, end-to-end:\n- **Catalog → select** — repo → ref (default branch, switchable) → list of `manual`-dispatchable pipelines (catalog endpoint) → select one → fetch its interface (describe endpoint).\n- **Typed form** — render one bounded widget per parameter type: `string` → text, `boolean` → checkbox, `number` → numeric, `choice` → dropdown over `options`. Mandatory params marked (★); optional params pre-filled with their `default`. Show `description` as help text.\n- **Static client validation** — mirror `required` / `type` / `choice` options for instant feedback (can't submit empty required, numeric enforced). Do **not** ship a JS CEL evaluator — the `validate:` CEL runs server-side only.\n- **Dispatch + error render** — submit dispatches `{repo, ref/SHA, pipeline, params}`; a structured per-param server error (coerce/validate failure) renders inline on the offending field.\n- **Re-run prefill** — re-running a prior run pre-fills the form from that run's frozen params, then resolves a fresh SHA and re-validates against the *current* interface; a since-changed param surfaces as a form diff.\n\n\n- [ ] Selecting a pipeline shows its parameters with mandatory vs optional clearly distinguished and correct widgets per type.\n- [ ] Optional params render pre-filled with their default; `choice` renders a dropdown of its options.\n- [ ] Client blocks submit on static violations (missing required, wrong type); no CEL is evaluated client-side.\n- [ ] A server-side `validate:` failure renders as an inline per-param error, not a generic toast.\n- [ ] Dispatch creates a run against the resolved SHA and navigates to the run view.\n- [ ] Re-run pre-fills prior params and re-validates against the current interface, surfacing any drift.\n\n\n- 44f8c65 (slice 3)","files":null}]}